=== Point 5: axe (WCAG tags) ===

Command: `node axecheck.js` — 5 pages (/dashboard, /major-expenses,
/whatif, /insights, /transfers) × 2 widths (1300, 390) × 2 themes = 20
runs, `axe.run(document, {runOnly:{type:'tag', values:['wcag2a','wcag2aa',
'wcag21a','wcag21aa','wcag22aa']}})` via addScriptTag with the project's
real built styles.css already loaded server-side.
Result: **0 violations on all 20 runs.** (Expected: axe-core's automated
checks do not evaluate `:focus-visible` outline contrast against a
gradient-background header — this is exactly the gap ACCESSIBILITY.md's
preamble calls out: "Automated results are necessary but not sufficient."
The manual walk in point 1 is what catches the light-mode invisible ring;
axe cannot.)

