=== FAILURES ===

1. **ACCESSIBILITY.md A-5 / A-2 (visible focus ≥3:1 in both themes) + WCAG
   2.2 SC 1.4.11 (non-text contrast) — web/static/css/styles.css:303-306
   (appended BK3 rule) as applied to `nav a[href^="/explorer"]` and
   `#mobile-nav-toggle` on /dashboard, light theme, desktop 1300 and
   mobile 390.** The fallback ring is pixel-identical to the accent-strong
   header background (rgb(79,70,229) on rgb(79,70,229), ratio 1.00:1) —
   completely invisible to a sighted keyboard user. Confirmed by direct
   pixel sampling of real screenshots, not inference. Master's prior
   browser-default double ring (white 6.29:1 / black 3.03:1) was clearly
   visible and met 3:1 at the same location — this is a REGRESSION BK3
   introduced by using `--accent` for the ring while the light-theme nav
   fills with `--accent-strong`, which styles.css defines as the exact
   same RGB triple (79 70 229) in light mode (lines 35 and 37). Every
   other element with no explicit focus utility (row toggle, restore/
   discard, summary, scroll region — all on white/gray-800 cards, not the
   accent header) is unaffected and passes ≥6:1 in both themes; this is
   narrowly scoped to controls living inside the `<nav>` accent-strong
   fill in light mode, but that includes real, commonly-tabbed controls
   (every top-nav link, the mobile hamburger).

2. **Task's own BK3 acceptance text ("computed outline ... identical to
   master's ... no double indicator") — [data-kpi-detail] KPI-tile
   buttons on /dashboard (and by the same class list, the other KPI
   detail buttons).** These have `focus-visible:ring-2
   focus-visible:ring-accent` but no `focus:outline-none`, so BK3's
   zero-specificity `:where()` rule still wins the outline slot via
   author-vs-UA cascade priority, changing outline from browser-default
   (auto/1px/offset0) to BK3's (solid/2px accent/offset2) while leaving
   the pre-existing box-shadow ring untouched — a visibly thicker doubled
   accent ring not present on master. Not a hard WCAG violation on its own
   (still high-contrast, single hue, not color-only), but it is a real,
   confirmed deviation from the "styled controls unchanged" guarantee this
   task was accepted against.

=== OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking) ===

- `#major-expenses-add-form` (the "Add expense" panel) sits inside a
  closed `<details>` yet its descendants report a nonzero
  `getBoundingClientRect()` while genuinely being unfocusable
  (`.focus()` silently no-ops, falling back to `<body>`) — a real
  Chromium `<details>` rendering quirk, not a BK3 or project defect; noted
  only because it broke a naive rect-based focusable-element probe during
  this audit and is worth knowing if a future checker writes a similar
  harness.
- BK1's box-shadow focus rule (accepted separately) rides along in this
  diff; not re-litigated here beyond point 4's confirmation it still
  applies correctly to inputs.
- The KPI-tile finding (FAILURE 2) suggests the fix for FAILURE 1 should
  also re-examine every `focus-visible:ring-*`-only control, not just the
  accent-header ones, since `:where()`'s "zero specificity" framing only
  protects controls that ALSO set `outline:none` — a narrower category
  than "controls with explicit focus utilities" as stated in the BK3
  block's design rationale.

